## Key Analysis Findings

* Petrol showed a balanced overall performance for daily mixed driving.
* E85 had a lower fuel price but a higher cost per kilometer due to reduced mileage.
* EV produced the lowest CO₂ emissions among all fuel types.
* Diesel demonstrated competitive running costs but comparatively higher emissions.
* CNG offered economical running costs while maintaining relatively low emissions.
* Maintenance costs generally increased as vehicle age increased.
* The generated dashboard clearly highlighted fuel cost comparisons, maintenance trends, environmental impact, and E85 break-even calculations using interactive SVG charts.

